---
import ContentPage from "../layouts/ContentPage.astro";
import { ORG_EMAIL } from "../lib/seo";

const site = "https://refocus.co.in";
const UPDATED = "2026-10-14";
const mailto = `mailto:${ORG_EMAIL}?subject=Delete%20my%20Refocus%20account`;
const title = "Delete your Refocus account";
const description =
  "How to delete your Refocus account and data, what gets deleted, and what is kept.";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    name: "Delete your account — Refocus",
    url: `${site}/delete-account`,
    description,
    dateModified: new Date(UPDATED).toISOString(),
  },
];
---

<ContentPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="/delete-account"
  heading="Delete your Refocus account"
  updated={UPDATED}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>
    You can permanently delete your Refocus account and its data at any time.
    Deletion is immediate and can't be undone.
  </p>

  <h2>Delete in the Refocus app</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the Refocus app and sign in.</li>
    <li>Go to <strong>Profile → Account → Delete account</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      Tick <em>“I understand that my account and all of its data will be
      permanently deleted”</em>.
    </li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Delete account permanently</strong> and confirm.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Delete on the website</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Sign in at <a href="https://dashboard.refocus.co.in">dashboard.refocus.co.in</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Open <strong>Settings → Danger zone → Delete account</strong>.</li>
    <li>Type <strong>DELETE</strong> to confirm.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Either way, your account is deleted straight away and you're signed out.</p>

  <h2>Can't sign in? Request deletion by email</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a> from the email address on your
    account with the subject “Delete my Refocus account”. We'll confirm and
    delete the account within 7 days.
  </p>

  <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your account and profile: name, username, email, password, and
      sign-in connections (Google, Apple)
    </li>
    <li>Your preferences and matching answers (gender, generation, focus areas)</li>
    <li>Friends, friend requests, and direct messages</li>
    <li>Session requests, and sessions only you were booked into</li>
    <li>Your community posts, comments, and likes</li>
    <li>Your blocks and personal task lists</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is kept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Sessions you shared with a partner</strong> stay in your
      partner's history, with you removed from them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Messages you sent in the shared community chat</strong> stay
      visible but are shown as “Deleted user”, without your name or photo.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A limited safety record</strong>: your email, name, username, IP
      addresses, the dates you joined, last signed in and deleted your account,
      and whether your account was restricted. We keep this to prevent abuse,
      such as banned users signing up again. It is not used for anything else.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anonymous usage analytics</strong> and records we are legally
      required to keep may be retained.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Questions? Contact <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>. See also our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
